1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:11,052
Meet NightShift, an autonomous on-call engineer. It catches production failures, tests a fix on a shadow copy, and applies it only when it is proven, with no human paged.

2
00:00:12,317 --> 00:00:19,310
The overview shows live health, time to heal, and an action budget, so the agent can never start a restart storm.

3
00:00:20,570 --> 00:00:30,247
The service map blames the deepest failing service, the root cause, instead of restarting every symptom. And this panel counts what a blind auto-restart would have done wrong.

4
00:00:31,504 --> 00:00:40,667
Now the Workspace. Here you bring your own app. This is a small Express bookstore API, in a real editor with a terminal and a request runner.

5
00:00:41,931 --> 00:00:48,745
We start it from the terminal. Traffic flows through NightShift's proxy, so the app needs no code changes.

6
00:00:50,006 --> 00:00:55,300
Every endpoint is discovered from the code. One click sends a request through the proxy.

7
00:00:56,551 --> 00:01:06,069
Now let's break it. AI inject bug picks a random route and a random kind of bug. An AI writes the bug, and it is checked on a throwaway copy first.

8
00:01:07,330 --> 00:01:21,401
The AI, groq, broke orders.js. Within seconds NightShift sees /authors and /books and /books/featured and /orders and /orders/summary and / and /health failing and opens an incident.

9
00:01:22,665 --> 00:01:35,133
It tests fixes on shadow copies with replayed production traffic. A restart won't help, because the bug is in the code. So it asks the AI to write a fix, using the error logs and the exact change.

10
00:01:36,388 --> 00:01:44,401
The AI fix passed the shadow test, so NightShift applied it. Here is the bug on the left, and the fix groq wrote on the right.

11
00:01:45,655 --> 00:01:54,058
It watches production for twenty seconds to confirm the fix holds, then writes a Heal Receipt: what broke, what was tried, and what was applied.

12
00:01:55,308 --> 00:02:02,036
Every detection, verdict and action lands in the audit log, so you can see exactly what the agent did, and why.

13
00:02:03,291 --> 00:02:09,225
That's NightShift. Detect, test on a shadow copy, fix, and prove it.
